feat(web): API tokens page (mint, list, revoke)

The v0.3 ApiToken entity has a REST surface, but the only
client was a curl smoke test. Add the user-facing page so
humans can mint, see, and revoke their tokens without leaving
the Web app.

What changed:
- New Page Pages/ApiTokens.razor: lists every token owned by
  the current user (with prefix, scopes, created/last-used/
  revoked timestamps), shows an "Active" / "Revoked" badge,
  exposes a mint form (name + read/write scope checkboxes), and
  a one-shot secret panel that surfaces the cleartext secret
  exactly once at issuance with a "I've copied it" dismiss.
- New ISecurityApiClient (Services/Api/SecurityApiClient.cs)
  with ListTokensAsync, IssueTokenAsync, RevokeTokenAsync.
  Mirrors the rest of the typed-client surface.
- Three new DTOs in Shared/ApiDtos.cs: ApiTokenSummaryDto,
  ApiTokenIssuanceDto, IssueApiTokenRequestDto.
- NavMenu gets an "API tokens" link under Workspaces for
  authenticated users.
- wwwroot/css/app.css gets styles for the page-hint, scopes
  row, issued-secret warning panel, secret box, token list.
- Program.cs registers ISecurityApiClient in DI.

Verified: 187 unit + 20 integration tests still green. Build
passes with no warnings; the Blazor output bundle picks up
the new page and the new CSS rules.
